from pathlib import Path
import json,html
R=Path(__file__).resolve().parent
s=json.loads((R/'SUMMARY.json').read_text())
rows=''.join('<tr>'+''.join('<td>'+html.escape(str(v))+'</td>' for v in [x['regime'],f"{x['flags']}/200",x['not_estimable'],x['informative_median'],x['criterion_pass']])+'</tr>' for x in s['results'] if x['view']=='exact_body')
body='''<!doctype html><meta charset="utf-8"><title>Line and position qualification</title><style>body{font:17px/1.55 system-ui;max-width:1050px;margin:40px auto;padding:20px;background:#f7faf8;color:#193c30}td,th{padding:9px;border-bottom:1px solid #bdcfc5;text-align:left}table{border-collapse:collapse}a{color:#176b53}</style>
<h1>Nuisance controls pass; broad power qualification fails</h1>
<p>Frozen synthetic qualification: 1,800 fresh datasets, two views, all 3,600 results preserved. No manuscript files read or rescored. H/F remain separate in any future protocol.</p>
<h2>What changed</h2><p>The test selects disjoint rectangles spanning two lines and two exact interior positions, within page, line length and matching body. Selection uses coordinates and bodies, never prefix labels or qok outcomes. Only alternating sh/ch arrangements can flip. Every flip preserves both lines' prefix composition and both positions' prefix counts; qok placements remain fixed. The primary also preserves exact-body composition. Remaining cells are pinned.</p>
<p>The conditional null is computed exactly over independent rectangle orientations with integer-count convolution. There is no Monte Carlo tail uncertainty or mixing assumption. Bonferroni8 is retained for prospective panels/readings/views. This conditions on more information than the earlier test and consequently discards much of the usable variation.</p>
<table><tr><th>Primary control</th><th>Flags</th><th>Not estimable</th><th>Median informative rectangles</th><th>Frozen gate</th></tr>'''+rows+'''</table>
<p>All five nuisance regimes meet the required Wilson95 upper false-flag bound of .05. Strong dense positives meet the lower power bound of .80. The smaller effect (a 15-percentage-point conditional increase, not calibrated to Voynich) detects 60%, with Wilson95 interval 53.1–66.5%. Sparse strong positives detect 0%; 65/200 have no informative rectangle. Even the dense strong positive uses a large 45-point effect. These findings do not establish power for manuscript-sized effects or support.</p>
<h2>Failure retained</h2><p>Overall status: FAIL. The frozen small-effect and sparse-power requirements do not pass. A limited success against these nuisance generators is not authorization to rescore Voynich. No thresholds were relaxed and no post-outcome revision was fitted.</p>
<h2>Ending fix and verification</h2><p>The previous eey/ey merge is fixed: edy, eey, ey and y remain disjoint with longest-match priority. Explicit tests include all four endings and a nonmatching word. Small exact-distribution examples agree with exhaustive enumeration; all encountered flips preserve row and column counts, and direct scores agree with the analytic contrast. Frozen hashes remain unchanged.</p>
<p>These generators use one body per ending, so the two views coincide. Their agreement is not independent evidence, and broader ending matching across different bodies has not been power-qualified here. The synthetic engine also does not exercise a corpus tokenizer, unknown-token handling, variable-length parsing or an H/F loader.</p>
<p>Exchangeability is justified for the tested additive-logit line/position/page settings; arbitrary line-by-position interactions are not ruled out. Rejection would still indicate conditional association, not grammar or meaning.</p>
<p>The next useful development target is a better-supported conditional randomization that uses more legal arrangements while preserving both margins. Any such method needs an exact or independently validated null and fresh sparse-power controls. That revision is not implemented here.</p>
<p><a href="PROTOCOL.json">Frozen rules</a> · <a href="FREEZE.json">Freeze hashes</a> · <a href="SUMMARY.json">Results and intervals</a> · <a href="TRIALS.json">All trials</a> · <a href="VERIFICATION.json">Verification</a></p>'''
(R/'report.html').write_text(body,encoding='utf-8')
assert all((R/p).exists() for p in ['PROTOCOL.json','FREEZE.json','SUMMARY.json','TRIALS.json','VERIFICATION.json'])
print('Report saved; local links checked. Visual rendering not inspected.')
